---
title: Steak au Poivre with Miso-Mushroom Sauce
description: Classic au poivre with the cognac swapped for an umami-rich miso and mushroom cream sauce.
course: main
cuisine: french
servings: 2
time_active: 35
time_total: 60
leftovers: poor
tags: [date-night]
pairs: [roasted-asparagus]
---

Pat @filet mignon{2}(6 to 8 oz each, or NY strip) dry. Press @black pepper{}corns{2%tbsp}(coarsely crushed) and @kosher salt{1%tbsp} into both sides. Rest at room temperature ~{15%minutes}.

Heat @butter{1%tbsp} and @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #skillet{} over medium-high. Sear the steaks ~{3-4%minutes} per side for medium-rare (135°F). Move to a plate to rest.

== Miso-Mushroom Sauce ==

In the same skillet, melt @butter{1%tbsp} and cook @shallot{1}(minced) and @mixed mushrooms{2%cups}(sliced shiitake, cremini, or oyster) ~{5%minutes}.

Add @dry white wine{1/2%cup}, scrape up the browned bits, and reduce by half, ~{5%minutes}.

Stir in @white miso{1%tbsp} and @heavy cream{1/2%cup} and simmer until thickened, ~{3-4%minutes}.

Slice the steaks and spoon the sauce over.
